<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!-- OUTGOING EMAIL: whose name is at the bottom.

         THE DEFECT, measured on the demo tenant by posting a real invoice to
         its customer with the context `account.move.send` uses
         (account/models/account_move_send.py:558,
         `email_notification_allow_footer=True`):

             Powered by <a href="https://www.odoo.com?utm_source=db&amp;utm_medium=email"
                           style="color: #875A7B;">Odoo</a>

         That line is in the mail sent to the CLIENT'S CUSTOMER, over the
         client's name, with the client's invoice attached. It is the most
         externally visible surface in the product and nothing had looked at it.

         WHOSE NAME BELONGS HERE — deliberately NOT the same answer as the
         backend footer.

         The backend footer is Sapian's, from constants a tenant cannot edit,
         because that surface is OUR product being used by the client's staff:
         they know what they bought, and a client rewriting our support number
         would be a defect. This email is a different thing. It is the CLIENT's
         commercial correspondence to THEIR customer — a document about a debt
         owed to the client, not about our software. So the two halves are
         separated:

         1. "Powered by Odoo" is simply WRONG, and goes unconditionally. It
            attributes the client's business software to a vendor that is not
            us, and links the client's own customer into a competitor's
            marketing funnel (`utm_source=db&amp;utm_medium=email`). No licence
            requires it — the position is in README.md, "Odoo attribution":
            `mail` is LGPL-3, GPL-3 §5(d) covers Appropriate Legal Notices, and
            a UTM-tagged marketing link is not one.

         2. "Powered by SapianERP" replaces it, ON BY DEFAULT, and the client
            can switch it off (`res.company.sapian_email_attribution`).
            On by default because this is the highest-reach surface we have and
            a white-label ERP vendor is normally discovered exactly here.
            Switchable because it rides on the client's letterhead: a trading
            company emailing a formal invoice has a legitimate say in what that
            document advertises, in a way it does not have over the chrome of
            software it licences from us. "Ours, always" would be taking a
            decision that is not ours to take; "nothing at all" would give up
            the reach for no gain to anyone.

            Off means OFF — the line disappears. It never falls back to Odoo.

         WHERE. Two layouts carry it:
           * mail.mail_notification_layout — every message_post notification,
             so the invoice and the quotation, both of which pass
             `email_notification_allow_footer=True` (account_move_send.py:558,
             sale_order.py:1077).
             `mail.mail_notification_layout_with_responsible_signature` is a
             PRIMARY inheritance of it and picks this up for free — which
             matters, because that is the layout invoices actually use
             (`_get_mail_layout`, account_move_send.py:583).
           * mail.mail_notification_light — the compact layout, used by the
             payment receipt.

         THE XPATH IS THE ANCHOR'S PARENT, not the div's position. The obvious
         `//div[@t-if='show_footer'][2]` is positional and there are two such
         divs; `//a[contains(@href, 'odoo.com')]/..` names the one node that can
         only be this one. Same matched-by-href reasoning as the login page.

         AND IT REPLACES THE WHOLE CONTAINER, not just the anchor, because the
         words "Powered by" sit OUTSIDE the anchor in upstream's markup — so
         removing the anchor alone would leave a dangling "Powered by" on a
         company that switched the attribution off. The container also holds the
         UNFOLLOW link, which is a real feature and is carried across unchanged.

         THE BUTTON COLOUR IS NOT FIXED HERE. Every template involved reads
         `company.email_secondary_color or '#875A7B'`, so setting that one field
         fixes the button everywhere at once — including templates this file
         does not touch, such as the portal invitation and the password reset.
         See models/res_company.py. -->

    <template id="mail_notification_layout_sapian"
              inherit_id="mail.mail_notification_layout"
              name="SapianERP: outgoing mail attribution">
        <xpath expr="//a[contains(@href, 'odoo.com')]/.." position="replace">
            <div t-if="show_footer" style="color: #555555; font-size:11px;">
                <t t-if="company.sapian_email_attribution">
                    Powered by <a target="_blank" href="https://sapiantech.com"
                                  t-att-style="'color: ' + (company.email_secondary_color or '#14454F') + ';'"
                                  >SapianERP</a>
                </t>
                <span t-if="show_unfollow" id="mail_unfollow">
                    <t t-if="company.sapian_email_attribution"> | </t>
                    <a href="/mail/unfollow" style="text-decoration:none; color:#555555;">Unfollow</a>
                </span>
            </div>
        </xpath>
    </template>

    <template id="mail_notification_light_sapian"
              inherit_id="mail.mail_notification_light"
              name="SapianERP: outgoing mail attribution (compact layout)">
        <xpath expr="//a[contains(@href, 'odoo.com')]/.." position="replace">
            <td align="center" style="min-width: 590px;">
                <t t-if="company.sapian_email_attribution">
                    Powered by <a target="_blank" href="https://sapiantech.com"
                                  t-att-style="'color: ' + (company.email_secondary_color or '#14454F') + ';'"
                                  >SapianERP</a>
                </t>
                <span t-if="show_unfollow" id="mail_unfollow">
                    <t t-if="company.sapian_email_attribution"> | </t>
                    <a href="/mail/unfollow" style="text-decoration:none; color:#555555;">Unfollow</a>
                </span>
            </td>
        </xpath>
    </template>

</odoo>
